  "term": "behavioral psychology",
  "definition": "Behavioral psychology, in this learning context, is a way of understanding how people’s perceptions and habits are linked to what they actually do. It emphasizes how factors such as trust, reliance, and critical participation can shape learning behaviors, engagement, and persistence.",
